{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7nj5uytdtk3sthj5bp4xfusnmcu4tfvhfc57xneafbv73oi3ipuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases passed, and **no change to the Rust translation was required** — it was already correct.\n\n## What the library is\n\nOne C translation unit, one public symbol: `void driver(int x)` → prints `2*x + 300`. `objdump` confirms straight-line wrapping 32-bit arithmetic (`add %eax,%eax` / `addl $0x12c`), which is exactly what the Rust `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add` reproduce.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapping\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` on both `.so`s. C exports exactly one API symbol (`driver`); Rust exports it too. Symbol diff empty; no untranslated module, no stubs. All Rust undefined symbols are libc/libgcc and resolve (`dlopen(RTLD_NOW)` succeeds).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 12 rows. Mechanical grep proves the error surface is *empty* (no `return`, assert, range/null check, or branch at all), so rows 1–4 prove that absence differentially and 5–12 cover the reachable generic boundaries (`INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, one-step-past-wrap, garbage upper 32 bits of the argument register, unsigned bit patterns).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 19 rows. The option axis is empty (no flags/handles/globals); rows enumerate the input-shape and stream-state axes.\n- **Feature combos**: Cargo.toml has no `[features]` and CMake has no options ⇒ exactly one configuration. `run_all_feature_combos.sh` derives this mechanically and runs check+build+test for the empty combo, the default set, and the release profile.\n\n## Phases B–D — results\nAll 19 CONFIGS rows, all 12 ERRORS rows, and 4 symbol-parity tests pass in every configuration. Tests load **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and compare stdout byte-for-byte; the Rust code is never called directly.\n\n**Exhaustive**: since the domain is just 2³², I closed it rather than sampled — 8 shards × 536,870,912 = **all 4,294,967,296 inputs byte-identical** (~13 min). Also verified against a gcc `-O3` C build (signed-overflow UB doesn't change codegen: `lea 0x12c(%rdi,%rdi,1),%esi`).\n\n## Three real bugs found — all in the harness, none in the translation\n1. **libtest parallelism** corrupted fd-1 captures → one `#[test]` per capturing binary, rows run via a `RowRunner` that still reports each row.\n2. **libtest's 60 s slow-test warning** injected exactly 68 bytes into captures, making every exhaustive shard \"diverge\" at ~60.3 s. Dumping bytes instead of hashes revealed `test <name> has been running for over 60 seconds`; the tell was that every line in that chunk is 10 bytes and 68 isn't a multiple of 10. Fixed by validating each capture against the C-required byte length and retrying, with **bisection to a single input** before declaring a divergence.\n3. **`SIGBUS`** from restaging `.so` copies over a file another process was executing → per-PID staging dir.\n\nMutation testing confirms the suite isn't vacuous: `+301`, non-wrapping arithmetic, and a dropped `\\n` are all caught; an i64-truncation mutant correctly passes (it's semantically equivalent); and a mutant wrong for *only* `x == 1234567891` survives a 4.2M-sample sweep but the exhaustive run pinpoints it exactly — which is why the exhaustive pass matters."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":823,"cache_read_input_tokens":181382,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":823,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6782de2-2435-4b23-b3fd-d8aaae7fb4e8","uuid":"6e4e2fb8-8f87-44fa-9485-dd0a94e40039","timestamp":"2026-08-18T15:00:34.300Z"}
